diagram application "Notification bus — roles, with the leaving side pinned"

# `queue-roles.cairn` with one addition: each endpoint names a *side* as well as
# its role. The two suffixes accumulate and answer different questions — the
# role says which cap of the queue the flow meets (`producer` left, `consumer`
# right), the side which edge of its own element it leaves from. Written in
# either order: `CAPTURE.producer.top` and `VALIDATE.top.producer` both read as
# a producer leaving the top.
#
# The producers here leave upward and the consumers downward, so the two groups
# separate above and below the bus instead of fanning out of the facing sides.
# See documentation/DSL_SPEC.md § Positioning controls

application ORDERS "Order platform" { logo: spring
  module CAPTURE  "Order\ncapture"
  module VALIDATE "Order\nvalidation"
}

queue QUEUE_NOTIF "Notification\nqueue" { logo: rabbitmq }

application MAILER "Mail sender" { logo: nodedotjs }
application PUSHER "Push sender" { logo: go }

CAPTURE.producer.top  -> QUEUE_NOTIF (AMQP)
VALIDATE.top.producer -> QUEUE_NOTIF (AMQP)

MAILER.consumer.bottom -> QUEUE_NOTIF (AMQP)
PUSHER.bottom.consumer -> QUEUE_NOTIF (AMQP)

legend {
  note "`.producer.top` is both: the queue's producer cap, left from the element's top edge"
}
